Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• `applicant_full_name` (bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.products_23) : identify the exact company name; we will keep only rows where this value is **exactly** `'SanofiAventis'`.  
• `product_id` (products_23 / products) : key that connects a product row to the formulation tables and therefore to each molecule (`molregno`).  
• `approval_date` (products_23 / products) : the marketing‑approval date; we will later aggregate with MAX() to keep only the latest date per molecule.  
• `trade_name` (products_23 / products) : commercial name; will be listed together with the latest approval date for each molecule.  
• `molregno` (formulations_23 / formulations) : ChEMBL’s molecule identifier; provides the “molecule” we need.  
Conditions that will be used  
• `applicant_full_name  =  'SanofiAventis'` – exact, case‑sensitive match (no other field will be used to infer the company).  
• An equality join on `product_id` between products_23 and formulations_23.  
• A GROUP BY / DISTINCT to collapse multiple approvals per molecule and retain only the most recent (`MAX(approval_date)`).  

Below are 10 exploratory‑to‑final BigQuery SQL snippets (each different, each limited to 20 rows) that gradually reach the requested result.

```sql
-- 1) Quick look at all products whose applicant is exactly 'SanofiAventis'
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.products_23`
WHERE applicant_full_name = 'SanofiAventis'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Distinct trade names filed by 'SanofiAventis'
SELECT DISTINCT trade_name
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.products_23`
WHERE applicant_full_name = 'SanofiAventis'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Distinct product IDs for that company
SELECT DISTINCT product_id
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.products_23`
WHERE applicant_full_name = 'SanofiAventis'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Join each of those product IDs to formulations_23 to discover molecules (molregno)
SELECT p.product_id,
       f.molregno
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.products_23` AS p
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.formulations_23` AS f
  ON p.product_id = f.product_id
WHERE p.applicant_full_name = 'SanofiAventis'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Distinct molecules (molregno) linked to SanofiAventis
SELECT DISTINCT f.molregno
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.products_23`  AS p
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.formulations_23` AS f
  ON p.product_id = f.product_id
WHERE p.applicant_full_name = 'SanofiAventis'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Molecule, trade name and approval date (raw duplicates kept)
SELECT f.molregno,
       p.trade_name,
       p.approval_date
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.products_23`  AS p
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.formulations_23` AS f
  ON p.product_id = f.product_id
WHERE p.applicant_full_name = 'SanofiAventis'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Latest approval date per molecule (no trade name yet)
SELECT f.molregno,
       MAX(p.approval_date) AS latest_approval
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.products_23`  AS p
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.formulations_23` AS f
  ON p.product_id = f.product_id
WHERE p.applicant_full_name = 'SanofiAventis'
GROUP BY f.molregno
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) For each molecule, keep only rows whose approval_date equals the latest
WITH latest AS (
  SELECT f.molregno,
         MAX(p.approval_date) AS latest_approval
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.products_23`  AS p
  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.formulations_23` AS f
    ON p.product_id = f.product_id
  WHERE p.applicant_full_name = 'SanofiAventis'
  GROUP BY f.molregno
)
SELECT l.molregno,
       p.trade_name,
       l.latest_approval
FROM latest AS l
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.products_23` AS p
  ON p.approval_date = l.latest_approval
 AND EXISTS (
       SELECT 1
       FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.formulations_23` AS f
       WHERE f.product_id = p.product_id
         AND f.molregno  = l.molregno
     )
WHERE p.applicant_full_name = 'SanofiAventis'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Same goal but using ARRAY_AGG to pick one trade_name (if multiples share the max date)
SELECT molregno,
       ARRAY_AGG(trade_name ORDER BY trade_name LIMIT 1)[OFFSET(0)] AS trade_name,
       latest_approval
FROM (
  SELECT f.molregno,
         p.trade_name,
         p.approval_date,
         MAX(p.approval_date) OVER (PARTITION BY f.molregno) AS latest_approval
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.products_23`  AS p
  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.formulations_23` AS f
    ON p.product_id = f.product_id
  WHERE p.applicant_full_name = 'SanofiAventis'
)
WHERE approval_date = latest_approval
GROUP BY molregno, latest_approval
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) FINAL ANSWER: all distinct molecules developed by 'SanofiAventis',
-- listing one trade name and the most recent approval date for each molecule
WITH joined AS (
  SELECT
    f.molregno,
    p.trade_name,
    p.approval_date
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.products_23`  AS p
  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.formulations_23` AS f
    ON p.product_id = f.product_id
  WHERE p.applicant_full_name = 'SanofiAventis'
),
ranked AS (
  SELECT
    molregno,
    trade_name,
    approval_date,
    RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY molregno ORDER BY approval_date DESC, trade_name) AS rnk
  FROM joined
)
SELECT
  molregno,
  trade_name,
  approval_date AS latest_approval_date
FROM ranked
WHERE rnk = 1
ORDER BY molregno
LIMIT 20;
```

Each snippet is capped at 20 rows with `LIMIT 20` purely for inspection; remove or raise that limit when you need the full list.
